  "result": "I'd make it so changing your mind doesn't cost you anything. Right now, admitting you were wrong often feels like losing status, loyalty, or your identity, so people dig in, defend bad positions, and keep fighting over things they'd drop if they could. Plenty of wars, family feuds, and public pile-ons run on that.\n\nIf being wrong felt survivable, a lot of conflicts would shrink. People could say \"I didn't know that\" or \"you convinced me\" without flinching, and the people around them would treat it as a good thing rather than a betrayal. I think that would quietly fix more problems than most grand schemes.",
